From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kill: include <sys/pidfd.h> when UL_HAVE_PIDFD

util-linux 2.38 configure enables UL_HAVE_PIDFD when <sys/pidfd.h>
exists (glibc >= 2.39, e.g. Ubuntu 24.04) but never includes the
header, so pidfd_open()/pidfd_send_signal() are implicit declarations
and gcc-14 rejects them as errors.  Older glibc never has the header
so UL_HAVE_PIDFD stays off and this include is compiled out there.

Backport of upstream 2.38.1 fix.

Signed-off-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 misc-utils/kill.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/misc-utils/kill.c
+++ b/misc-utils/kill.c
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@
 #ifdef UL_HAVE_PIDFD
 # include <poll.h>
+# include <sys/pidfd.h>
 # include "list.h"
 struct timeouts {
 	int period;
